we basically knew that this would happen  step one was the faux vindication of  Donald Trump claiming to be totally  exonerated when Robert molars report  literally says it cannot exonerate  Donald Trump from obstruction of justice  and we've already talked about all the  other problems contained in the bar  report which I've now explained I think  enough times some on the Monday show  someone that's used they show some of  the ones they show that I'm not going to  go through it all in detail again today  but part of that framing of total and  unmitigated exoneration from Donald  Trump was that he was the victim of  something here  despite 37 indictments despite the  report saying that Moeller cannot  exonerate Donald Trump from obstruction  the framing that Donald Trump and the  people around him have adopted over the  last few days has been that the  investigation represents an unfair  politically partisan attack on the  President of the United States that was  phase one okay now they're moving on to  Phase two and we knew that phase two  would happen which is to start to accuse  those who investigated him individually  of wrongdoing and in particular Donald  Trump is now accusing some particular  FBI officials who investigated him of  treason which is a ridiculous standard  to try to apply to what they did in  carrying out their jobs for the federal  government but we'll get to that in a  second Donald Trump gave an interview to  Fox News to Sean Hannity of course this  was his first interview I think since  the Moller report was handed over to  William Barr on Friday and ultimately we  got the bar report the summary of a  summary on Sunday and in this interview  with Sean Hannity Donald Trump says that  individual FBI employees Peter struck  and Lisa page committed treason this is  the word that Donald Trump is using  treason  merely by participating in a legal FBI  investigation which is ridiculous is  kind of the only way I can say it take a  look at this clip from the interview  last night it was many months before  that that straat can page we're talking  about the insurance policy right an  insurance policy just in case  Hilary Clinton lost they wanted an  insurance policy against me and what we  were playing out until just recently was  the insurance policy they wanted to do a  subversion it was treason it was really  treason if the Republican Party had done  this to the Democrats if we had done  this to President Obama you'd have a  hundred people in jail right now and it  would be treason it would be considered  treason and they'd be in jail for the  rest of their lives  funny that he mentions if this was Obama  right  imagine if what we have seen between  Trump and Russia we had seen between  Obama and Iran that's actually the Obama  comparison that seems most relevant to  me which I actually saw a James Comey  bring up in an interview yesterday I  believe it was and it can be really easy  to lose sight of the facts when Trump is  kind of hurling these generalized  allegations in this way you have to  break it down into individual sort of  practical answerable questions was the  investigation illegal of course it  wasn't the answer is no was the  investigation started on some kind of  partisan pretense or with no probable  cause no and in fact the more we learn  about the more we realize all of the  probable cause that sort of served as a  catalyst for this investigation to get  going from the beginning so then we get  to did individuals break the law by  being employed by the FBI and doing the  work that they were told to do in terms  of this investigation of course they  didn't and then we get to the  allegations specifically of treason  which is the crime of betraying one's  country by especially by attempting to  kill the sovereign or to overthrow the  government that's not what an FBI  employee participating in a legal  investigation is guilty of obviously  that is not treason and when Donald  Trump just throws out the nonsense in  this way in unfortunately kind of works  and I hope that most people and I know  that I'm kind of preaching to the choir  here in our audience I think people  understand working for the FBI and doing  what you're  sign to do is not treason but I know for  sure that I will start getting  voicemails and tweets and emails from  Trump is saying it was treason David  what the FBI investigators did was  treason because it was part of an  attempt to overthrow the administration  of the president Donald Trump and that's  why this is unfortunately effective when  Donald Trump goes on Fox News and he  comes up with this stuff the FBI agents  who were doing the investigation or  treasonous it filters down there is  actually a sort of trickle-down effect  and I don't know you know in five or ten  years how is this entire fiasco going to  be remembered I don't know the answer to  that but I do believe that it's  important not to forget forget that we  had the Trump Tower Moscow deal we had  Trump firing the FBI director and  admitting it was to stop the probe Trump  calling for Russians to hack Hillary's  emails which they did or maybe had  already done and Trump knew it at that  point in time  Trump associates meeting with Russians  in Trump Tower we all know what we saw  we also knew that Trump personally  colluding was not going to be the  outcome certainly not at least rising to  criminality we were all saying that for  more than a year at this point in time  so the result of the probe that is no  collusion charges against Trump really  does come away it was predictable and it  was common sense from the beginning but  my concern here is the total  whitewashing of the bigger picture  because the investigations continue  Muller did indict 37 people I believe it  is we need to get a full copy of the  report and when we allow things to sort  of slide in the direction of crazy and I  would say the individuals doing the  investigation being treasonous falls  under the umbrella of crazy it makes it  really difficult to actually communicate  the truth of what took place and is  still taking place and this is why I  said at the top of the show I was  thinking yesterday is it even worth  bothering like is it even worth  researching and putting together stories  about  why the bar letter is a joke and why the  legalese is pointing to deception  because once again I think a lot of our  audience gets it and the people that  don't are committed I don't know if 100  percent committed but 99.9% committed to  whatever framing they are accepting from  either Trump or from elements on the  left that they find appealing maybe it's  not worth it and I just shouldn't talk  about it anymore I don't know let me  know what you think does it make sense  to continue to try to break this stuff  down you can clean up your remote  control clutter with today's sponsor  control center by kaavo which simplifies  your home theater so you can control  everything connected to your TV with one  easy-to-use remote that has voice  control you can plug in your streamer  your sound system cable or satellite  your game console and the control center  will do it all stop fiddling with  different remotes or what I do often  breaking multiple remotes as I try to  figure out which is the right one no  weeding through messy search results to  get the content you want one universal  voice remote controls at all say what  you want to watch control center handles  the rest  take your at-home entertainment  experience from stressful to simple  enjoy what you want when you want it  I've set it up with my TV sound system  and DVD player it has made everything  much much simpler you can shop now and  get 40% off of control center with promo  code Pakman that's 59.95 40% off regular  pricing of 99.95 service plan required  first 45 days are free control center is  available at CAA vo comm and best buy  the control center by kaavo one remote  that does it all

